    {
      "finding_id": "F-GAP-002-01",
      "notes": "The snippet is quoted verbatim from sources/SRC-c52222b5.txt line 2 ('Ask for confirmation before an action that cannot be undone, and state the consequence in the dialog text, for example which package will be awarded and to whom.'). The claim is framed as what 'the fetched guidance says' and does not strengthen it. The recommendation applies it to DEC-001 (award is final): naming the package and supplier mirrors 'which package will be awarded and to whom', and saying the award is final is the consequence of this particular irreversible action. It answers GAP-002 research question 1.",
      "limitations": [
        "The source states 'This page is a test fixture for the Feature Research Agent and is not real documentation' (line 5). It is not GOV.UK, Atlassian or Material guidance, although the metadata labels it official_documentation.",
        "No publication date or version.",
        "Does not answer the WCAG 2.2 SC 3.3.4 question in GAP-002.",
        "The source does not say whether the confirmation must be a modal dialog or a separate page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-GAP-002-02",
      "notes": "The snippet is verbatim at sources/SRC-c52222b5.txt line 3 and the claim restates it without strengthening ('should be labelled with the action itself, such as Award package, rather than a generic OK'). It bears directly on the confirmation pattern asked about in GAP-002 research question 1.",
      "limitations": [
        "The source is a self-declared test fixture, not real documentation (line 5), and not an established design system.",
        "No publication date or version.",
        "This is guidance on wording only and is not a confirmed requirement for this product."
      ]
    },
    {
      "finding_id": "F-GAP-002-03",
      "notes": "The snippet is verbatim at sources/SRC-c52222b5.txt line 4 and the claim restates it faithfully. Combined with DEC-001 ('cannot be withdrawn, changed or undone by anyone'), undo is not available for an award, so the source's distinction places the award on the confirmation side. This is relevant to GAP-002's 'Destructive-action confirmation and undo' checklist item.",
